  "notes": "{寝坊|ねぼう} functions both as a noun and as a する verb. As a noun, it can mean the act of oversleeping or a person who habitually oversleeps.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {寝坊|ねぼう}する: to oversleep\n- {寝坊|ねぼう}して{遅刻|ちこく}する: to be late from oversleeping\n- {寝坊|ねぼう}してしまう: to end up oversleeping (unintentional)\n\nAS A NOUN (person):\n- あの{人|ひと}は{寝坊|ねぼう}だ: He's a late sleeper / sleepyhead.\n- {寝坊助|ねぼうすけ}: sleepyhead (playful/affectionate term)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {朝寝坊|あさねぼう}: sleeping in late in the morning (more specific)\n- {二度寝|にどね}: going back to sleep after waking up\n- {寝過|ねす}ごす: to oversleep, to sleep past (a stop on a train, etc.)\n\nFORMS:\n{寝|ね} (sleeping) + {坊|ぼう} (boy, fellow — often used for people with a habit).",
